<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afonso III of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1210–<a href="/years/1279">1279</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Afonso the Boulonnais</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Afonso III of Portugal was king from 1248 to 1279. He completed the Portuguese reconquest by taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faro">Faro</a> and the rest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> in 1249, and the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a> of 1267 settled the territory in Portugal's favour. He also strengthened royal government, summoned townsmen to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> and moved the court to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afonso-iii-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Afonso III of Portugal" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: cgb · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marabotin_%C3%A0_l%27effigie_d%27Alphonse_III_dit_le_Boulonnais_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
